student_response:
I see where I went wrong.  
When you divide a fraction by a whole number you don’t split the numerator and denominator by that number—you multiply by the reciprocal of the whole number.

So:

\[
\frac{6}{9}\div 3=\frac{6}{9}\times\frac{1}{3}
   =\frac{6}{27}
   =\frac{2}{9}
\]

That means the correct choice is **C.**  \(\frac{2}{9}\).  
Thanks for pointing out the mistake—I’ll remember to use the reciprocal next time.

