student_response:
I think I made a mistake by dividing both the top and bottom by 2. When you divide a fraction by a whole number you really have to *multiply* the whole fraction by the reciprocal of that number. So

\[
\frac{4}{8}\div 2=\frac{4}{8}\times\frac{1}{2}
=\frac{4\times 1}{8\times 2}
=\frac{4}{16}
=\frac{2}{8}
=\frac{1}{4}.
\]

So the correct choice is **B. \( \frac{2}{8}\)** (which can also be written as \( \frac{1}{4}\)). I’ll keep practicing this step so I don’t accidentally split the numerator and denominator when I shouldn’t.

