\[
\frac{4}{8} \div 2 \;=\; \frac{4}{8} \times \frac{1}{2}
  \;=\; \frac{4 \times 1}{8 \times 2}
  \;=\; \frac{4}{16}
  \;=\; \frac{1}{4}.
\]

In the answer choices that’s the same as \(\frac{2}{8}\) (which simplifies to \(\frac{1}{4}\)). So the correct choice is **B. \( \frac{2}{8} \)**. Thanks for catching that!

